.TH LIBMPQ__UPDATE_ADD_DATA 3 2026-10-12 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__update_add_data \- add an absent member to a staged MPQ update
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__update_add_data(mpq_update_s *" "update,"
.BI "        const char *" "filename, const uint8_t *" "data,"
.BI "        libmpq__off_t " "size, const mpq_file_options_s *" "options);"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Adds a new filename to the current staged namespace. Data and options are
borrowed only during the call; NULL options select native storage defaults.
NULL data is permitted for a zero-byte member. Removal followed by addition
of the same filename is supported. Replacement APIs remain replacement-only.
The original archive is unchanged until commit. Failures before staged ownership
transfer leave the previous stage available. If closing the previous stage fails
after rebuild validation, further mutation and commit are rejected; abort remains
safe and attempts temporary-file cleanup.
V3 rebuilds require complete filename reconstruction; see libmpq__update_begin(3).
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero on success or a negative libmpq error.
.SH ERRORS
Duplicate filenames return LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST. Reserved internal filenames or
unsupported source layouts return LIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT. Size, table-capacity,
allocation, encoding and I/O errors may also be returned.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq__update_add_path (3),
.BR libmpq__update_replace_data (3),
.BR libmpq__update_begin (3),
.BR libmpq__update_commit (3),
.BR libmpq__update_abort (3)
